        "original_id": "07407325-a639-5ee1-82f7-a1673c4615e6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elia Kazan, William Inge, David Amram, Zohra Lampert, Natalie Wood, Warren Beatty\n- Works: Splendor in the Grass, Let's Scare Jessica to Death\n- Topics: film production, acting careers, awards\n\nFacts:\n- Elia Kazan was born as Elias Kazantzoglou on September 7, 1909, and he died on September 28, 2003.\n- Elia Kazan was a Greek-American director, producer, writer, and actor.\n- The New York Times described Elia Kazan as one of the most honored and influential directors in Broadway and Hollywood history.\n- Zohra Lampert was born on May 13, 1937.\n- Splendor in the Grass is a 1961 Technicolor drama film about a teenage girl dealing with sexual repression, love, and heartbreak.\n- Splendor in the Grass was written by William Inge, directed by Elia Kazan, and scored by David Amram.\n- William Inge appears briefly in Splendor in the Grass as a Protestant clergyman.\n- William Inge won an Oscar for the screenplay of Splendor in the Grass.\n- Zohra Lampert starred alongside Natalie Wood and Warren Beatty in Splendor in the Grass.\n- Zohra Lampert played the title character in the 1971 cult horror film Let's Scare Jessica to Death.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
